ent": "enpe7n4le03ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extensible markup language", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a meta-language that allows to define programming languages according to software requirements.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When developers use this web framework, they should use Extensible Markup Language or Simple Object Access Protocol.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "simple object access protocol", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a protocol to interchange data between different web applications.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When developers use this web framework, they should use Extensible Markup Language or Simple Object Access Protocol.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "object-oriented programming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a programming language model based on objects and data.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're right!  They both work through object-oriented programming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ECMA", "type": "name"}, {"content": "European Computers Manufacturers Association, an organization to set standards for software. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(acronym)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, Microsoft is working with ECMA to standardize this programming language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about C# and another programming Language. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster with differences and similarities about these two programming languages.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your poster with the rest of the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for information about C# and another programming Language.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make poster with differences and similarities about these two programming languages.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my poster with the rest of the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals: Should and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Should</strong> and <strong>Would</strong> are both modal auxiliary verbs and they have different uses in English. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Use <strong>should</strong>  to give recommendations, advice or to express strong advice. Look at the examples: </br></br>  <i>Recommendation or Advice:</i></br></br>  <ul><li>You <strong>should</strong> use C# to create your software applications.</li> <li>They <strong>shouldn't</strong> have to worry about duplicating the code, they <strong>should</strong> use the existing code. </li></ul></br>   <i>Obligation:</i></br></br>  <ul><li>The developers <strong>should</strong> create a tutorial on how to use this programming language.</li>  <li> <strong>Should</strong> I have the .Net framework for being able to use C#?</li></ul></br>  <i>Expectation:</i></br></br>  <ul><li>The company <strong>should</strong> launch soon standardize versions of this programming language. </li> <li>The new versions <strong>shouldn't</strong> take too long. </li> <li>How long <strong>should</strong> we wait to have the most updated version?</li></ul></br>  <strong>Would</strong> can imply assumptions or requests. Some examples are listed below:  </br></br><i>Conditionals:</i></br></br> <ul><li>What <strong>would</strong> you do if you could have all the tool you need to create software in only one platform? </li> <li>If I were you, I <strong>would</strong> check how to use C# as soon as possible. </li> <li>It <strong>wouldn't</strong> be difficult to create new versions if all software companies get an agreement. </li></ul></br>  <i>Assumptions or expectations: </i></br></br>  <ul><li>It <strong>would</strong> be useful to have a standardize version of this language. </li> <li><strong>Would</strong> it be difficult to use it? </li></ul></br>  <i>Request:</i></br></br>  <ul><li><strong>Would</strong> you help me preparing my oral presentation about C sharp?</li></ul></br>   As modal auxiliary verbs, <strong>Should</strong> and <strong>Would</strong> have invariable forms and the main verb next to them always keeps its base form. Look at the following table to identify the structures for both of them:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Affirmative</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Negative</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Interrogative</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Should</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>You <strong>should</strong> use C# to create your software applications.</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>You <strong>shouldn't</strong> use C# to create your software applications.</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i><strong>Should</strong> you use C# to create your software applications?</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Would</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <i>It <strong>would</strong> be useful to have a standardize version of this language.</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <i>It <strong>wouldn't</strong> be useful to have a standardize version of this language.</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <i><strong>Would</strong> it be useful to have a standardize version of this language?</i>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "What would you do if you had the chance to build dynamic software applications only by using one programming language?   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why should we use it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When developers use this web framework, they should use Extensible Markup Language or Simple Object Access Protocol. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Wouldn't be better if there was a standard version of C sharp?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Common Content Words and Expressions Used in C#", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you are dealing with a specific topic in English, you should use precise vocabulary to contextualize the reader or listener.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This also happens when you are developing a text or conversation about C sharp. As it is a technical discipline, it is necessary to use key vocabulary related to this programming language. </br> In the table below, you will find a list of some words that may be useful for this topic:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Category</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Meaning</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Developer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\"